  "notes": [
    "Brings the estate to fifteen services and all four languages. Every template embeds its flag keys literally, carries the release, reproduces the same cluster weighting and business-hours batch sizing, and ships a Dockerfile. All three new templates were built and run against the live project in Dev before any repository was created.",
    "Deployment is unchanged in this step. Creating the repositories starts the GitHub indexing clock, which is the slow resource; wiring the new services into the evaluator set is a separate step so a container problem cannot delay indexing.",
    "demo-subscriptions, demo-identity and demo-support carry skipIndexingCheck: the tooling will never probe them by any method. They are the controls for the indexing experiment. Their unique flags are either never-started or also carried by an indexed repository, so no archive evidence depends on them.",
    "demo-sms-notifications finally gains a consumer here through demo-notifications, the TypeScript service. It was the one flag that would have accumulated nothing had TypeScript stayed source-only."
  ]
